# (format 36, the user's: "a page dedicated to the filter") the Chord filter page: ENV a third time (Chord, Chord voice,
# Chord filter, Chord FM, Chord LFO, back), its knobs Cutoff, Reso, Env, Env decay (P_CCUT 139, P_CRES 38, P_CENV 39,
# P_CEDEC 63); the Chord voice page Attack and Decay alone. Basic's own: Env -25, Env decay +31 (REPORT-stabenv)
listen
wait 3000
tap ENV
wait 300
expect view 1
tap ENV
wait 400
said Chord voice page, voice Saws: Attack 0, Decay 25
expect view 8
tap ENV
wait 400
said Chord filter page, voice Saws: Cutoff 0, Reso 0, Env -25, Env decay +31
expect view 31
expect par39 -25
expect par63 31
shot filter.png
# Env: up 10 (no notch on the way), then down to its left end (none: NO SWEEP on the picture)
spin K3 10
wait 300
expect par39 -15
said Env -15
expect bigring 1
spin K3 -100
wait 300
expect par39 -50
said Env -50
wait 2500
shot filter_nosweep.png
# Env decay: down 10, then up past the tie's notch at 0 is not needed: 31 -> 21 -> 50
spin K4 -10
wait 300
expect par63 21
said Env decay +21
spin K4 100
wait 300
expect par63 50
said Env decay +50
wait 2500
shot filter_slow.png
# Reso and Cutoff, as on the Chord voice page before
spin K2 -100
wait 200
expect par38 -50
said Reso -50
spin K1 -100
wait 200
expect par139 -50
said Cutoff -50
# the piece keeps them; the reset puts the recipe's back
turn PRESET 1
wait 400
turn PRESET -1
wait 400
expect par39 -50
expect par63 50
press GLO
wait 1700
release GLO
wait 300
expect par39 -25
expect par63 31
# ENV on: Chord FM, Chord LFO, back to Chord
tap ENV
wait 300
expect view 12
tap ENV
wait 300
expect view 22
tap ENV
wait 300
expect view 1
# held, a nudge: the page whose knob moved most (the voice, the filter or the FM page): here Env, the filter's
# (format 36, the user's: ENV's nudge moves Env and Env decay too)
press ENV
wait 700
release ENV
wait 300
said CHORD NUDGE Env amount
expect view 31
wait 6000
expect peak_db_max -0.5
